      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "IPv4 Addresses and the Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The 32-bit Address",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "IPv4 = ==32 bits== as **four octets** (0-255), dotted decimal",
                "Each octet is 8 bits, so 4 x 8 = 32",
                "Mask says where the {blue:network} part ends and the {orange:host} part begins"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "ip = '192.168.10.37'",
                "print('.'.join(f'{int(o):08b}' for o in ip.split('.')))"
              ],
              "note": "each octet as 8 bits"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "11000000.10101000.00001010.00100101"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Classful Ranges",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Class",
                "First octet",
                "Default",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "A",
                  "1-126",
                  "/8",
                  "unicast"
                ],
                [
                  "B",
                  "128-191",
                  "/16",
                  "unicast"
                ],
                [
                  "C",
                  "192-223",
                  "/24",
                  "unicast"
                ],
                [
                  "D",
                  "224-239",
                  "none",
                  "==multicast=="
                ],
                [
                  "E",
                  "240-255",
                  "none",
                  "reserved"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`127.x.x.x` is ==loopback==, which is why A stops at 126",
                "{red:Waste}: a /8 gives ~16M hosts even if you need **300**",
                "That waste is why ==CIDR== replaced classful addressing"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. CIDR Notation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "10.1.4.0/22",
                    "sub": "address/prefix",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "22 network bits",
                    "sub": "first 22 bits",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "10 host bits",
                    "sub": "32 - 22",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Prefix = network bits",
              "text": "**/N** means the first ==N bits== are the network; the remaining **32 - N** are host bits."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Subnet Masks and Network, Broadcast, Host Math",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Subnet Masks and Network, Broadcast, Host Math",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Mask and Host Math",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Prefix",
                "Mask",
                "Host bits",
                "Usable"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "/24",
                  "255.255.255.0",
                  "8",
                  "254"
                ],
                [
                  "/26",
                  "255.255.255.192",
                  "6",
                  "62"
                ],
                [
                  "/20",
                  "255.255.240.0",
                  "12",
                  "4094"
                ],
                [
                  "/30",
                  "255.255.255.252",
                  "2",
                  "2"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Mask = ==prefix bits set to 1==, rest 0",
                "{blue:Network} = IP AND mask (host bits all 0)",
                "{orange:Broadcast} = host bits all 1",
                "==Usable hosts== = `2^h - 2`, h = host bits"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Block Size and Worked Example",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Block size== = 256 − mask octet, in the interesting octet",
                "/26: 256 − 192 = 64, so blocks `.0` `.64` `.128` `.192`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "192.168.1.130/26",
                    "sub": "block 128",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Network",
                    "sub": "192.168.1.128",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broadcast",
                    "sub": "192.168.1.191",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hosts",
                    "sub": ".129 - .190",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Special Cases",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==/31==: point-to-point, 2 usable addresses (RFC 3021)",
                "==/32==: a single host route"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mind the -2",
              "text": "Usable is `2^h - 2`, not `2^h`: network and broadcast are reserved."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Interview Point**",
                "**Hosts in a /26?** 62 = 2^6 − 2",
                "**Network of 192.168.1.130/26?** 192.168.1.128, broadcast .191",
                "**Why does /31 work?** Point-to-point needs no broadcast (RFC 3021)"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Subnetting Workflow: Carving Networks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Subnetting Workflow: Carving Networks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Size, Borrow, List",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Step 1==: smallest `h` with 2^h - 2 >= hosts",
                "50 hosts: h=5 gives 30, ==h=6 gives 62==",
                "==Step 2==: prefix = 32 - h, so /26",
                "Borrow `n` bits for 2^n subnets: /24 borrow 2 = ==four /26s==",
                "==Step 3==: network = previous broadcast + 1"
              ],
              "style": "number",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Subnet",
                "Network",
                "Broadcast"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1",
                  "192.168.1.0/26",
                  ".63"
                ],
                [
                  "2",
                  "192.168.1.64/26",
                  ".127"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "192.168.1.128/26",
                  ".191"
                ],
                [
                  "4",
                  "192.168.1.192/26",
                  ".255"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. VLSM",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Sort",
                    "note": "largest need first",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Place",
                    "note": "aligned boundary",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Next",
                    "note": "previous broadcast + 1",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repeat",
                    "note": "smaller blocks",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Summarization",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==192.168.0.0/24 + 192.168.1.0/24 = 192.168.0.0/23==",
                "Only if ==contiguous== and ==aligned=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Not aligned",
              "text": "192.168.1.0/24 + 192.168.2.0/24 are adjacent but cannot form a /23."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**/27 hosts?** 30 (2^5 - 2)",
                "**VLSM order?** Largest first: stays aligned, no overlap",
                "**Merge two /24s?** Only if contiguous and aligned"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
