            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. NAT, IPv6, Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==NAT/PAT== rewrites private to public, PAT uses **ports**",
                "==IPv6== = 128-bit hex, `::` compresses one zero run",
                "IPv6 has **no broadcast** and needs **no NAT**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistakes",
              "text": "Forgetting the **-2** for usable hosts. Misaligned subnet boundaries. Treating `172.32.x.x` as private. Using `::` twice in one IPv6 address."
            }
